From 0afdee46583459484004bd79764dd81cd8c333d8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 14:30:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] build: real macOS pipe2/sem_init replacements, no compat
 headers

pipe2() doesn't exist on Darwin -- add a portable static inline
polyfill to util.h (pipe() + per-fd fcntl(F_SETFL/F_SETFD)), included
by all five call sites.

sem_init/sem_destroy are deprecated on Darwin, and documented as
outright unreliable there, not just discouraged. Use libdispatch's
plain-C semaphore API instead (dispatch_semaphore_create/_wait/
_signal/dispatch_release, no Objective-C/Blocks, available since the
first libdispatch release in macOS 10.6): terminal.h now conditions
its <semaphore.h> include and the render worker start/done fields'
type on __APPLE__, with render_sem_wait/render_sem_post wrapping
whichever API is in effect so terminal.c/render.c's call sites don't
need to branch individually.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01U6fuL1PtRJHhr97gAGyS1h
